# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin gives every page a browsing context
# group of its own. Nothing here needs a handle across that line: external links
# already carry rel="noopener", and /download is a plain link that redirects to
# GitHub in the same tab, not a popup reporting back through window.opener.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here, deliberately. It is hash-based and emitted per
# build as a meta tag (astro.config.mjs), so a static copy in this file would
# block the inline scripts of the next build, whose hashes differ.
#
# No `preload` on Strict-Transport-Security. The preload list takes registrable
# domains only, so on drakar.mgcrea.io the token would do nothing except suggest
# the site was on the list. Preloading belongs on mgcrea.io itself, if anywhere.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Everything under /_astro/ carries a content hash in its filename, so the URL
# changes whenever the bytes do. Without this, Workers Assets serves them with
# the same `max-age=0, must-revalidate` as the HTML, which puts a conditional
# request on the render-blocking stylesheet on *every* refresh: the round-trip
# that gave armada's buttons time to paint unstyled. See src/styles/tokens.css.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
